e>Biological and clinical relevance of the urokinase-type plasminogen activator (uPA) in breast cancer</article-title><source>Biomed Biochim Acta</source><year>1991</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>731</fpage><lpage>741</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Biomed Biochim Acta||50|731||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1801751</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schneider</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pollan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jimenez</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruibal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lucas</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Nu&#x000f1;ez</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanchez</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tejerina</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Histologic grade and CD44 are independent predictors of axillary lymph node invasion in early (T1) breast cancer</article-title><source>Tumor Biol</source><year>1999</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>319</fpage><lpage>330</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Tumor Biol||20|319||bib12|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schneider</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lucas</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanchez</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tejerina</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruibal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cellular accumulation of uPA&#x02013;PAI-1 and uPA&#x02013;PAI-2 complexes in early (pT1) breast cancer: a new link in the uPA&#x02013;uPAr&#x02013;PAI chain</article-title><source>In Vivo</source><year>2000</year><volume>14<